pachi-numba
===========

pachi-numba is a translation of the Go engine Pachi from C to Python
(compiled with numba). It is a work based on Pachi and is distributed
under the GNU General Public License version 2 (the file LICENSE), like
Pachi.

Original work
-------------

Pachi, version 11.99, as included in OpenAI's pachi-py 0.0.21
(https://github.com/openai/pachi-py), by Petr Baudis, Jean-loup Gailly and
the other authors listed in the file CREDITS (copied from that version).
Upstream: https://github.com/pasky/pachi.

Pachi's licence statement (from its README): "Pachi is distributed under
the GPLv2 licence (see the COPYING file for details and full text of the
licence); you are welcome to tweak it as you wish (contributing back
upstream is welcome) and distribute it freely, but only together with the
source code."

Changes (GPLv2 section 2a)
--------------------------

October 2026: the C code of Pachi's default "uct" engine and everything it
uses (board, random numbers, 3x3 patterns, tactics, playout policies,
tree search, priors, ownermap) was translated line by line to Python
(pachi_numba/), restructured for numba (arrays instead of pointers and
structs, explicit stacks instead of recursion, per-engine random state
instead of thread-local globals), and given a Python interface
(pachi_numba/player.py, pachi_numba/parallel.py). Every translated file
says which Pachi file it translates. reference/shim.c is a new C
interface used only by the tests. The C sources in reference/pachi_src/
are Pachi's, unmodified (build files and documents left out).
